  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1047 PM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nFREEZE POTENTIAL:\n\nAs the trough moves further east over the Midwest, high \npressure builds behind over the Great Basin and Intermountain \nWest forming a Rex Block heading into Friday with northerly flow\nover the region. Much colder air mass settles over the region \ntonight with lows in the 20s for the northwest Colorado valleys \n(Yampa River Basin) where a widespread hard freeze appears \nlikely. Other areas in a Freeze Warning tonight include the \nupper Colorado River valley (COZ008) from Glenwood to Avon and \nthe San Juan River Basin (COZ023). A Freeze Warning remains in \neffect for those same areas Friday night as well, so depending \non how widespread of a hard freeze occurs in these zones would \ndetermine whether additional freeze warnings are needed. Outside\nof these areas, temperatures will be cooler but not expecting \ntemperatures below freezing for the overnight. \n\nDRY THIS WEEKEND:\n\nHigh pressure moves overhead by Saturday as the Rex Block \nbreaks down and the low that was at the bottom of the Rex Block \nwill open up and pull enough moisture with it to bring isolated \nshowers to the San Juans as it tracks over the Four Corners \nSunday afternoon. This is fairly weak so not expecting much \nimpact but drier conditions overall this weekend with \ntemperatures around 5 degrees or so below seasonable. Isolated \nshowers are possible again over the high terrain Monday \nafternoon as southwest flow keeps the area a bit unsettled. \nTemperatures overall will bump up a little bit towards normal \nbut lean on the side of below seasonable for most areas. \n\nUNSETTLED WEATHER RETURNS MID TO LATE NEXT WEEK:\n\nThe next chance for impactful weather comes mid to late next \nweek beginning Tuesday as a low pressure system dives down the \nwest coast and forms a deep closed low over the Desert \nSouthwest. Diffluent southwest flow will allow for better \norographic showers Tuesday, more scattered over the high \nterrain. This low will track across the Great Basin and lift \nacross the area, currently timed late Wednesday through Friday \nof next week with cooler conditions returning and better chances\nof more widespread precipitation and mountain snow. Details are\nstill a bit uncertain with timing, amounts and how much cold \nair will arrive with this system but this mid to late next week \nsystem is one to keep an eye on.",
